  "description": "Structured concurrency for C# and .NET. Run tasks in parallel in a TaskGroup: the first failure cancels the rest, no task outlives the group, and you get the real error instead of a TaskCanceledException. Includes C# equivalents of JavaScript's Promise.all, Promise.any and Promise.allSettled (TaskGroup.AllAsync, FirstSuccessAsync and AllSettledAsync), a concurrency limit and rate limiting, timeouts that cancel the work (Kotlin's withTimeout), hedged requests, Erlang-style supervisors that restart failing work, bounded parallel streams of results, chunking by size and time, per-key sequencing, Go's singleflight, Go's select for System.Threading.Channels, and OpenTelemetry tracing and metrics.",
